  "description": "Open a legacy binary Excel workbook (.xls, BIFF8: Excel 97-2003) as an ordinary XlsxDocument (DocWright.Spreadsheet) and save it as .xlsx; managed .NET, no Office, no interop, no need for the DocWright Word package. Reads sheets, cell values, formulas (shared and array formulas included), names, number formats, fonts, fills, borders, alignment, merged cells, column widths, row heights, hidden rows and columns and frozen panes; what it does not read (charts, drawings, notes, pivot tables, macros and others) is reported. Read only; hostile input bounded.",
